    <!-- ===================================================================
         Archetypes for EXISTING BASEGAME props, not for assets we built.

         Most GTA interior furniture is absent from the global model index:
         its archetype is declared inside the owning interior's .ytyp (the
         extracted v_int_40.ytyp holds 75 `v_40_*` archetypes for the hospital
         alone) and that ytyp is only resident when its MLO is. So
         IsModelInCdimage returns false and /prop reports "Invalid model" even
         though the name is right and the asset is in the game files.

         Declaring the archetype ourselves puts the name back in the index. The
         drawable and its textures are already streamable; only the archetype
         record was missing. This mirrors exactly how the hospital's own ytyp
         declares them: ASSET_TYPE_DRAWABLE, assetName == name, no
         drawableDictionary. physicsDictionary is left EMPTY, unlike our own
         props: their collision lives in the game files, not in imperial_props.

         Two values here are deliberately provisional:

         * textureDictionary is EMPTY, to test whether these props carry their
           textures embedded in the .ydr. If one spawns untextured, its txd name
           (Forge lists it, e.g. the hospital props all share
           'v_40_hospital_txd') goes in here.
         * bounds are generous placeholders. A prop still spawns with wrong
           bounds, which only drive culling, so an over-large box is harmless
           while an under-large one pops out of view at odd angles. Spawn each
           one, read the true size off /propinfo, then tighten these.

         Caveat worth knowing: if one of these interiors ever DOES load nearby,
         two archetypes will exist for the same name. That is tolerated, but
         ours would be the wrong-bounds one, so tighten them before shipping.
         =================================================================== -->

